-- title:
--   Étale coordinate on a formally smooth local algebra of relative dimension one
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring and $S$ a commutative local ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure whose structure map $A \to S$ is a local homomorphism, and assume $S$ is formally smooth and essentially of finite type over $A$. Suppose further that the induced map from $A$ to the residue field of $S$ is surjective, and that the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{S/A}$ has rank one as an $S$-module (its `Module.finrank` over $S$ equals $1$). Then there exists an element $t$ of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_S$ of $S$ such that: the ring homomorphism underlying the $A$-algebra map $A[X] \to S$ sending $X \mapsto t$ (evaluation at $t$) is both formally smooth and formally unramified; and $\mathfrak m_S$ equals the sum of the ideal generated by $t$ and the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$ of $A$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_S = (t) + \mathfrak m_A S$. The two smoothness conclusions are stated for the ring homomorphism $A[X] \to S$, not as an assertion about an $A[X]$-algebra instance.
--
--   This is the local form of the structure theory of a smooth morphism of relative dimension one at a point with residue field coming from the base: such a local algebra admits an étale coordinate $t$, and $t$ is a uniformiser of the fibre over the closed point of $A$. It is used in the construction of étale coordinates at smooth points of a semistable model of a curve, via [`AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.exists_etaleCoordinate_localRing_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.exists_etaleCoordinate_localRing_of_mem_smoothLocus); the formal smoothness and unramifiedness of evaluation at $t$ are obtained from the criterion that every differential in $\Omega_{S/A}$ is uniquely an $S$-multiple of $\mathrm{d}t$.
-- source:
